    {
      "text": "Lord … has wrought so many miracles, 1 Ne. 17:51. should the … miracles be wrought among other nations, 2 Ne. 10:4. working mighty miracles, 2 Ne. 26:13 (Mosiah 3:5; 8:18; 15:6; Hel. 16:4). I am a God of miracles, 2 Ne. 27:23. power of God working miracles in them, Alma 23:6. began to be … greater miracles wrought, 3 Ne. 1:4. many miracles in the name of Jesus, 3 Ne. 8:1. I could not show unto them so great miracles, 3 Ne. 19:35. opened the eyes of their blind and unstopped the ears, 3 Ne. 26:15. wo unto him that shall say … there can be no miracle, 3 Ne. 29:7. in nothing did they work miracles save it were in the name of Jesus, 4 Ne. 1:5. God has not ceased to be a God of miracles, Morm. 9:15 (9:7–25). say that Jesus Christ did not do many mighty miracles, Morm. 9:18. ceaseth to do miracles … dwindle in unbelief, Morm. 9:20. if there be no faith … God can do no miracle, Ether 12:12. who wrought miracles wrought them by faith, Ether 12:16. have miracles ceased because Christ hath ascended, Moro. 7:27. by faith that miracles are wrought, Moro. 7:37. to another, that he may work mighty miracles, Moro. 10:12.",
